 "brief": "Healthy LLMs? Benchmarking LLM Knowledge of UK Government Public Health Information — As Large Language Models (LLMs) become widely accessible, a detailed un- derstanding of their knowledge within",
 "extended": "**Healthy LLMs? Benchmarking LLM Knowledge of UK Government Public Health Information**\n\n*BENCHMARKING LLM KNOWL-*\n\n27 pp, 41 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** As Large Language Models (LLMs) become widely accessible, a detailed un- derstanding of their knowledge within specific domains becomes necessary for successful real world use. This is particularly critical in the domains of medicine and public health, where failure to retrieve relevant, accurate, and current infor- mation could significantly impact UK residents. However, while there are a num- ber of LLM benchmarks in the medical domain, currently little is known about LLM knowledge within the field of public health. To address this issue, this pa- per introduces a new benchmark, PubHealthBench, with over 8000 questions for evaluating LLMs’ Multiple Choice Question Answering (MCQA) and free form responses to public health queries.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Introduction; Related work; MCQA LLM evaluations; Synthetic MCQA datasets; Public health evaluations; Methods; UK public health information; Pre-processing and chunking; Question generation; Automated MCQA error detection and sampling; Final MCQA benchmark dataset; Human expert quality assurance; Model evaluation approach; Benchmark subsets; Results; Human baseline; Experimental setup",
